From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 13:31:47 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 23/40] PROTOTYPE pvr: no 8- or 16-bit formats in the linear
 window-size rule

Local fix to the linear window-size rule, never to be sent (Imagination
declines LLM-generated code in src/imagination).

Linear R8 images sample wrong on a GX6250: Firefox uploads software-decoded
video as three R8 planes, and with them linear the video showed at half size
in the top-left quadrant with the rest clamped (or garbled). Exempting 1-byte
formats fixed it, 2 of 2 runs each way. The same images sample right on a
GE8300 (linear R8 1280x720 read back exactly), so the cause is the GX6250 or
Firefox's upload path; not found.

Keep 8- and 16-bit formats twiddled. An earlier version kept everything but
32-bit formats twiddled; on the GE8300 (844 MiB) that padded mpv's
RGBA16F/RGBA32F render targets to powers of two, 371 MiB of images for a
720p file instead of 182 MiB, and its first run ran the system out of
memory. 32-bit and wider formats take the rule (wider ones went linear
without trouble on both GPUs before: RGBA32F in Firefox on the GX6250, every
format on the GE8300 for weeks).

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_image.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_image.c b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_image.c
index f7614994fb0..5ef5cc12ac1 100644
--- a/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_image.c
+++ b/src/imagination/vulkan/pvr_image.c
@@ -62,6 +62,16 @@ static bool pvr_image_twiddle_padding_is_wasteful(const struct pvr_image *image)
        image->vk.array_layers > 1 || image->vk.samples > VK_SAMPLE_COUNT_1_BIT)
       return false;
 
+   /* Not for 8- and 16-bit texels: a linear R8 image sampled wrong on a
+    * GX6250 (Firefox's software-decoded video planes came out at half size,
+    * the rest clamped); 16-bit is untested there. 32-bit and wider formats
+    * take the rule: window-sized RGBA8 and D24S8/D32 buffers, and the
+    * RGBA16F/RGBA32F render targets of renderers such as mpv's, which padded
+    * to powers of two doubled mpv's GPU memory on a 1 GiB GE8300.
+    */
+   if (vk_format_get_blocksize(image->vk.format) < 4)
+      return false;
+
    return util_next_power_of_two64(w) * util_next_power_of_two64(h) * 4 >
           w * h * 5;
 }
